 ## 2026-07-20
 
+### 1145 — libssh2 adapter remains blocked on server-rekey observability and keepalive replies (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- BLOCKER: The accepted `libssh2_session_rekey` fork clears client byte/time/manual trigger initiation only. The exact public header exports no KEX lifecycle callback or generation query. Pinned libssh2 handles inbound `SSH_MSG_KEXINIT` entirely inside private `packet.c`/`transport.c` state, so the adapter cannot truthfully emit `.serverInitiated`, mark `activeKeyExchange`, increment generation, or distinguish server-KEX success/failure through the public boundary.
+- BLOCKER: `libssh2_keepalive_send` writes `keepalive@libssh2.org` with `want_reply=1` but returns after queueing and stores no outstanding request or reply outcome. The public API exposes no generic reply-requiring global request or request-success/failure correlation. Consequently the adapter cannot measure reply RTT, enforce reply timeout/miss allowance, or distinguish acknowledgement from silence.
+- EVIDENCE: The public macOS XCFramework exports only `libssh2_session_rekey`, `libssh2_keepalive_config`, and `libssh2_keepalive_send` among relevant symbols. `keepalive.c:52-96` contains no reply wait/state; inbound server rekey is private at `packet.c:1336-1369` and `transport.c:407-425,1039-1048`. Trace callbacks are unavailable in non-debug builds and are not a supported protocol API.
+- ROUTING: Do not report these gates green or build a mock-only partial adapter. Recommend a separately reviewed minimal fork extension exposing typed server-KEX lifecycle plus a nonblocking reply-correlated global-request/keepalive API; alternatives are explicitly failing the libssh2 candidate or revising the mandatory contract. Exact options and resume decision are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_server-rekey-keepalive-blocker.md`.
+
 ### 1115 — Minimal libssh2 public client-rekey fork clears the adapter blocker (TASK-260720-3vwls7)
 - DECISION: Pinned libssh2 `a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719` carries one allowlisted two-file patch: `include/libssh2.h` publicly declares `libssh2_session_rekey`, and `src/session.c` adds a null-checked, nonblocking-friendly `BLOCK_ADJUST` wrapper over the existing `ssh2_kex_exchange(session, 1, &session->startup_key_state)`. No crypto, algorithm, packet, channel, or private-header surface changed.
 - SUPPLY CHAIN: The builder verifies libssh2 and OpenSSL 3.5.7 archive SHA-256 values before extraction or patch application, checks source-license hashes, rebuilds five static Apple architecture slices, emits the combined BSD-3-Clause/Apache-2.0/acknowledgement notice, and fails closed on patch/hash/path drift. Two clean rebuilds produced byte-identical XCFramework artifact locks.

Stopped at an evidence-backed public-API boundary. The accepted client-rekey patch does not provide mandatory server-KEX observability or reply-confirmed keepalive semantics; implementation would require an additional reviewed fork decision or a contract/candidate decision.
  ✓ Confirm accepted dependency decisions and inspect the common SSH/native seams
  • Implement the named libssh2 adapter and deterministic unit tests
  • Run formatting, tests, boundary checks, and Apple build matrix
  ✓ Attach evidence, update board checklist/logbook, and hand off to review
